==Supporters and rivalries==
[[File:Stadin Kingit.jpg|thumb|HIFK Fotboll supporters June 2017.]]

Historically, HIFK was primarily a club for the [[Swedish-speaking Finns|Swedish-speaking population]] in Helsinki. Nowadays the club is bilingual. The most renowned supporter group of the club was ''Stadin Kingit'' (in English: ''"the kings of Stadi"''). Its name was derived from the common slang nickname for Helsinki (Stadi). Many members attend the handball, [[HIFK Bandy|bandy]] and [[HIFK (ice hockey)|ice hockey]] matches of [[HIFK]] as well.

The single most important fixture for HIFK supporters is against the major local rivals, [[HJK Helsinki|HJK]]. The fixture is commonly known as the [[Stadin derby]] and was last played during the [[Veikkausliiga]] season of 2022.

==Club structure==

HIFK Fotboll operate a large number of teams including 3 men's teams, 3 women's teams, 1 men's veterans team, 16 boys' teams and 5 girls' teams.

*''' HIFK''' competes in Group B of [[Kolmonen]] (Fifth tier) administered by the [[SPL Uudenmaan piiri|SPL Uusimaa]]. 
* ''' HIFK / 3''' competes in Group 4 of [[Vitonen]] (Seventh tier) administered by the [[SPL Uudenmaan piiri|SPL Uusimaa]].

